      "license_url": "https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0/",
      "retrieved": "2026-10-09",
      "revision": 106360894,
      "text": "コウスイガヤ は、セイロン島原産のイネ科オガルカヤ属の多年生植物の種。シトロネラグラスとも呼ばれる。"
    },
    "en": {
      "source": "Wikipedia 英語版「Cymbopogon nardus」",
      "source_url": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Cymbopogon_nardus",
      "license": "CC BY-SA 4.0",
      "license_url": "https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0/",
      "retrieved": "2026-10-09",
      "revision": 1271120428,
      "text": "Cymbopogon nardus, common name citronella grass, is a species of perennial aromatic plant from the family Poaceae, originating in tropical Asia. C. nardus cannot be eaten because of its unpalatable nature and is an invasive species that renders pastureland useless, since cattle will starve even in its abundance."
    }
